+     * (e.g. {@code List<Foo> foo}), the external id describes the runtime type
+     * of every element, not of the (List-typed) property value itself; the type
+     * deserializer's base type is the element type (`Foo`), so it cannot be
+     * invoked directly on the whole buffered value. Instead defer to the
+     * property's own {@code CollectionDeserializer}, substituting a type
+     * deserializer that already knows the id for each element -- this way the
+     * Collection deserializer still handles both a JSON Array of elements and,
+     * via {@code JsonFormat.Feature.ACCEPT_SINGLE_VALUE_AS_ARRAY}, a single
